# Project Description

- Kadodo is a web-based identity verification service provider for businesses and individuals in Africa.
- Kadodo requires users to create an account, and subscribe to one of their pricing plans to avail various identity verification workflows. Kadodo intends to serve the entire African continent, but because of country specific data protection and storage policies and other customizations, Kadodo will be offered over separate,  country specific sites. Each verification workflow (attached to a price plan) will be tied to a data-capture workflow, presented to the user as steps. E.g. Business information, certifications, details of promoters etc. The workflow and form controls for each step is controlled by a no-code workflow builder, authored by the Kadodo administrator.
- The application also includes a no-code website builder with sections for authring pages on the website, and managing navigation flows.
- Once a user starts the sign-up and identity workflow process, Kadodo will send notifications and updates via email. Users will be able to login to their account to track progress, or update their information.
- A submitted verification workflow is then routed to an appropriate verification agent (an admin console user), who will then verify individual parts of the application. Upon successful verification, users will be supplied with a verified Kadodo badge, which can be downloaded, printed, orchard on social media. The badge will have QR code or another mechanism to get to a limited transcript summary of the company’s current verification status.
- Verification will expire upon completion of the term, and the user may need to make a new verification application, or make a part-update and resubmit for re-verification. Even if no changes are present, the user will be able to pay the fee and extend the validity of their “Verified Kadodo” badge. The user/business will be assigned a unique KadodoID

