# Technical Details

1. Page Builder

* Core Structure
    ~ The page builder is a modular system that allows creating customizable pages using React blocks. Here's how it's organized:


* Data Model ( [page_interfaces.ts](mdc:resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/page_interfaces.ts) )
    ~ [PageBuilderCreate.tsx](mdc:resources/js/Pages/PageBuilder/PageBuilderCreate.tsx) interface defines the main page structure with:
      - Basic metadata (id, title, description, URL)
      - Publishing status
      - Blocks collection


* Block System
    ~ Each page consists of multiple blocks (PageBlock interface in [page_interfaces.ts](mdc:resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/page_interfaces.ts))
    ~ Blocks have common configurations (BlockConfiguration in [page_interfaces.ts](mdc:resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/page_interfaces.ts)):
        - Padding and margin controls
        - Responsive width settings (mobile, tablet, laptop, desktop)

    ~ Each block has:
        - Unique ID
        - Position for ordering
        - Block name for identification


* Multilingual Support
    ~ The system supports multilingual content through TextData interface [page_interfaces.ts](mdc:resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/page_interfaces.ts) :
        - English content
        - Malayalam content (optional)

    ~ Text fields use this structure for internationalization


* Rich Content Types
    The system supports various content types [page_interfaces.ts](mdc:resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/page_interfaces.ts):
    - BlockImage : For image content with URL and captions
    - BlockVideo: For video content with URL and MIME type
    - LinkData: For internal/external links
    - ItemListField: For managing lists of items (generic type)


* Page Builder Components
    The UI is organized into several components:

      - [PageBuilderCreate.tsx](mdc:resources/js/Pages/PageBuilder/PageBuilderCreate.tsx): Entry point for creating new pages
      - [PageBuilderEdit.tsx](mdc:resources/js/Pages/PageBuilder/PageBuilderEdit.tsx) : For editing existing pages
      - [PageBuilderIndex.tsx](mdc:resources/js/Pages/PageBuilder/PageBuilderIndex.tsx) : List view of pages
      - [UIBuilderPage.tsx](mdc:resources/js/Pages/PageBuilder/UIBuilderPage.tsx) : UI builder interface
      - [ViewBuilderPage.tsx](mdc:resources/js/Pages/PageBuilder/ViewBuilderPage.tsx) : Page preview component


* Module Organization
    The code is organized into several directories:
      - /resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/Blocks : Contains individual block implementations
      - /resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/Components: Reusable UI components
      - /resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/Pages: Page-level components
      - /resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/hooks: Custom React hooks for page builder functionality


* Block Customization
    Blocks are highly customizable with:

      - Responsive settings
      - Spacing controls
      - Content management
      - Media integration
      - Link management

* Example Block Type
    The ImageBlock in [page_interfaces.ts](mdc:resources/js/Modules/PageBuilder/page_interfaces.ts) interface shows a typical block structure:
      - Title (multilingual)
      - Description (list of multilingual text)
      - Image with caption
      - Optional video
      - Links and categories
      - Date information



# Customer Sign up

1. A user registers as a customer using the /sign-up/create url
2. Verifies the email using /verify-otp url.Generated otp will be available at o_t_p_s table against the email id
3.After verification, the user will be added as a customer in the customer table


# Customer workflow
1. A registered user can choose a price plan once logged in, using /choose-price-plan url. once a price plan is selected, the customer is tied to the price plan in the table custome_price_plans.
2. Price plans are associated with a workflow. Based on the price plan customer is to initiate the associated workflow and fill in the details using the url /customer-workflow-create.Once that is done the table customer_workflows table will be populated.





